        -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the power is given "If the claimant's address is not in Northern Ireland"; the text is silent on a claimant whose address is
        IF `the claimant's address is in Northern Ireland` THEN NOTHING
        OTHERWISE `sch 11 there is a right of appeal, on the shared reading of the requirement of consideration first` `the regulations require consideration of revision before an appeal` `the decision-maker has considered whether to revise the decision` `the consideration satisfied the further conditions the regulations specify`

